# 必考词 Unit25
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit25核心词汇

{{exception}}{{/ɪkˈsepʃn}}{{n. 例外； exception}}{{Most students passed the exam, with one exception.}}
{{excess}}{{/ɪkˈses}}{{n./adj. 过量； excess；超额的}}{{An excess of sugar is bad for your health.}}
{{exclude}}{{/ɪkˈskluːd}}{{v. 排除； exclude；排斥}}{{The price excludes tax and delivery charges.}}
{{execute}}{{/ˈeksɪkjuːt}}{{v. 执行； execute；处决}}{{The plan was executed flawlessly.}}
{{exempt}}{{/ɪɡˈzempt}}{{adj./v. 免除的； exempt；豁免}}{{Students under 18 are exempt from the tax.}}
{{exert}}{{/ɪɡˈzɜːt}}{{v. 施加； exert；运用}}{{The government exerted pressure on the company.}}
{{exhibit}}{{/ɪɡˈzɪbɪt}}{{v./n. 展览； exhibit；显示}}{{The museum exhibits rare artifacts.}}
{{expand}}{{/ɪkˈspænd}}{{v. 扩展； expand；膨胀}}{{The company plans to expand into Asian markets.}}
{{expedition}}{{/ˌekspɪˈdɪʃn}}{{n. 远征； expedition；考察}}{{They went on an expedition to the North Pole.}}
{{expense}}{{/ɪkˈspens}}{{n. 费用； expense；代价}}{{The project was completed at great expense.}}
{{expertise}}{{/ˌekspɜːˈtiːz}}{{n. 专业知识； expertise}}{{She has expertise in artificial intelligence.}}
{{explicit}}{{/ɪkˈsplɪsɪt}}{{adj. 明确的； explicit；清楚的}}{{The instructions were explicit and easy to follow.}}
{{exploit}}{{/ɪkˈsplɔɪt}}{{v./n. 开发； exploit；剥削}}{{The company exploited natural resources.}}
{{explore}}{{/ɪkˈsplɔːr}}{{v. 探索； explore；考察}}{{The children explored the forest.}}
{{explosion}}{{/ɪkˈspləʊʒn}}{{n. 爆炸； explosion；激增}}{{There was a population explosion in the 20th century.}}
{{export}}{{/ɪkˈspɔːt}}{{v./n. 出口； export}}{{The country exports oil to many nations.}}
{{expose}}{{/ɪkˈspəʊz}}{{v. 暴露； expose；揭露}}{{The report exposed the corruption in the government.}}
{{extend}}{{/ɪkˈstend}}{{v. 延伸； extend；扩展}}{{The deadline has been extended by one week.}}
{{extent}}{{/ɪkˈstent}}{{n. 程度； extent；范围}}{{The extent of the damage is still being assessed.}}
{{external}}{{/ɪkˈstɜːnl}}{{adj. 外部的； external；外面的}}{{The external walls of the building need painting.}}
{{extra}}{{/ˈekstrə}}{{adj./n. 额外的； extra；附加物}}{{You need to pay extra for the service.}}
{{extract}}{{/ɪkˈstrækt}}{{v./n. 提取； extract；摘录}}{{The machine extracts juice from the fruit.}}
{{extraordinary}}{{/ɪkˈstrɔːdnri}}{{adj. 非凡的； extraordinary；特别的}}{{She has extraordinary talent in music.}}
{{extreme}}{{/ɪkˈstriːm}}{{adj./n. 极端的； extreme；极端}}{{The weather has been extremely hot this summer.}}
{{fabric}}{{/ˈfæbrɪk}}{{n. 织物； fabric；结构}}{{The fabric of society is changing rapidly.}}
{{facilitate}}{{/fəˈsɪlɪteɪt}}{{v. 促进； facilitate；使容易}}{{Technology facilitates communication.}}
{{factor}}{{/ˈfæktər}}{{n. 因素； factor；因子}}{{Several factors contributed to the decline.}}
{{faculty}}{{/ˈfæklti}}{{n. 全体教员； faculty；能力}}{{The faculty voted to change the curriculum.}}
{{fade}}{{/feɪd}}{{v. 褪色； fade；逐渐消失}}{{The color faded after years of exposure to sunlight.}}
{{failure}}{{/ˈfeɪljər}}{{n. 失败； failure；故障}}{{Failure is a part of learning.}}
{{fancy}}{{/ˈfænsi}}{{adj./v./n. 花哨的； fancy；想象}}{{She wore a fancy dress to the party.}}
{{fatal}}{{/ˈfeɪtl}}{{adj. 致命的； fatal}}{{The accident was fatal to three passengers.}}
{{favor}}{{/ˈfeɪvər}}{{n./v. 赞同； favor；偏爱}}{{The judge ruled in favor of the defendant.}}
{{feasible}}{{/ˈfiːzəbl}}{{adj. 可行的； feasible}}{{The plan is technically feasible.}}
{{feature}}{{/ˈfiːtʃər}}{{n./v. 特征； feature；以…为特色}}{{The phone has many useful features.}}
{{federal}}{{/ˈfedərəl}}{{adj. 联邦的； federal}}{{The federal government controls the military.}}
{{fierce}}{{/fɪəs}}{{adj. 激烈的； fierce；凶猛的}}{{There is fierce competition in the market.}}
{{figure}}{{/ˈfɪɡər}}{{n./v. 数字； figure；认为； figure out}}{{The figure shows a significant increase.}}
{{finance}}{{/ˈfaɪnæns}}{{n./v. 财政； finance；资助}}{{The project was financed by the government.}}
{{fine}}{{/faɪn}}{{n./v. 罚款； fine；好的}}{{He was fined for parking illegally.}}
{{firm}}{{/fɜːm}}{{adj./n. 坚定的； firm；公司}}{{She works for a law firm.}}
{{fiscal}}{{/ˈfɪskl}}{{adj. 财政的； fiscal}}{{The government introduced new fiscal policies.}}
{{fix}}{{/fɪks}}{{v. 修理； fix；固定}}{{The mechanic fixed the engine.}}
{{flaw}}{{/flɔː}}{{n. 缺陷； flaw；裂纹}}{{The plan has a serious flaw.}}
{{flee}}{{/fliː}}{{v. 逃跑； flee；逃离}}{{The refugees fled the war-torn country.}}
{{flexible}}{{/ˈfleksəbl}}{{adj. 灵活的； flexible；可弯曲的}}{{The company offers flexible working hours.}}
{{float}}{{/fləʊt}}{{v. 漂浮； float；提出}}{{The idea was floated at the meeting.}}
{{flock}}{{/flɒk}}{{n./v. 群； flock；聚集}}{{A flock of birds flew over the lake.}}
{{flourish}}{{/ˈflʌrɪʃ}}{{v. 繁荣； flourish；挥舞}}{{The business flourished under her leadership.}}
{{fluctuate}}{{/ˈflʌktʃueɪt}}{{v. 波动； fluctuate}}{{Prices fluctuate throughout the year.}}
{{focus}}{{/ˈfəʊkəs}}{{v./n. 集中； focus；焦点}}{{We need to focus on the main issue.}}
{{forbid}}{{/fəˈbɪd}}{{v. 禁止； forbid}}{{Smoking is forbidden in the building.}}
{{forecast}}{{/ˈfɔːkɑːst}}{{v./n. 预测； forecast；预报}}{{The weather forecast predicts rain tomorrow.}}
{{formal}}{{/ˈfɔːml}}{{adj. 正式的； formal；形式上的}}{{The invitation is for a formal dinner.}}
{{format}}{{/ˈfɔːmæt}}{{n./v. 格式； format；格式化}}{{Please save the document in PDF format.}}
{{formula}}{{/ˈfɔːmjələ}}{{n. 公式； formula；方案}}{{The mathematical formula is easy to remember.}}
{{foster}}{{/ˈfɒstər}}{{v. 培养； foster；收养}}{{The program fosters creativity in children.}}
{{foundation}}{{/faʊnˈdeɪʃn}}{{n. 基础； foundation；基金会}}{{The theory has no scientific foundation.}}
{{fraction}}{{/ˈfrækʃn}}{{n. 分数； fraction；一小部分}}{{Only a fraction of the students passed the exam.}}
{{framework}}{{/ˈfreɪmwɜːk}}{{n. 框架； framework；体制}}{{The policy provides a framework for decision-making.}}
{{frequency}}{{/ˈfriːkwənsi}}{{n. 频率； frequency}}{{The frequency of earthquakes has increased.}}
{{friction}}{{/ˈfrɪkʃn}}{{n. 摩擦； friction；冲突}}{{There is friction between the two departments.}}
{{frontier}}{{/frʌnˈtɪər}}{{n. 边界； frontier；前沿}}{{Space is the final frontier.}}
{{frustrate}}{{/frʌˈstreɪt}}{{v. 使沮丧； frustrate；挫败}}{{The lack of progress frustrated the team.}}
{{fulfill}}{{/fʊlˈfɪl}}{{v. 履行； fulfill；实现}}{{She fulfilled her childhood dream of becoming a doctor.}}
{{function}}{{/ˈfʌŋkʃn}}{{n./v. 功能； function；运转}}{{The function of the heart is to pump blood.}}
{{fundamental}}{{/ˌfʌndəˈmentl}}{{adj. 基本的； fundamental；根本的}}{{Freedom of speech is a fundamental right.}}
{{furnish}}{{/ˈfɜːnɪʃ}}{{v. 提供； furnish；装备}}{{The apartment is fully furnished.}}
{{furthermore}}{{/ˌfɜːðəˈmɔːr}}{{adv. 此外； furthermore；而且}}{{The plan is expensive; furthermore, it is impractical.}}
{{gaze}}{{/ɡeɪz}}{{v./n. 凝视； gaze}}{{She gazed at the sunset.}}
{{generate}}{{/ˈdʒenəreɪt}}{{v. 产生； generate；引起}}{{The wind turbines generate electricity.}}
{{generous}}{{/ˈdʒenərəs}}{{adj. 慷慨的； generous；大量的}}{{She is generous with her time and money.}}
{{genius}}{{/ˈdʒiːniəs}}{{n. 天才； genius}}{{Einstein was a genius in physics.}}
{{genuine}}{{/ˈdʒenjuɪn}}{{adj. 真正的； genuine；真诚的}}{{The painting is a genuine masterpiece.}}
{{gesture}}{{/ˈdʒestʃər}}{{n./v. 姿态； gesture；做手势}}{{He made a gesture of goodwill.}}
{{global}}{{/ˈɡləʊbl}}{{adj. 全球的； global；全面的}}{{Climate change is a global issue.}}
{{govern}}{{/ˈɡʌvən}}{{v. 统治； govern；管理}}{{The country is governed by a democratic system.}}
{{grab}}{{/ɡræb}}{{v. 抓取； grab；吸引}}{{She grabbed her bag and ran out the door.}}
{{grace}}{{/ɡreɪs}}{{n. 优雅； grace；恩典}}{{She moved with grace and confidence.}}
{{gradually}}{{/ˈɡrædʒuəli}}{{adv. 逐渐地； gradually}}{{The situation is gradually improving.}}
{{grant}}{{/ɡrɑːnt}}{{v./n. 授予； grant；补助金}}{{The university received a research grant.}}
{{graphic}}{{/ˈɡræfɪk}}{{adj./n. 图形的； graphic；图表}}{{The report includes graphic illustrations.}}
{{grasp}}{{/ɡrɑːsp}}{{v./n. 理解； grasp；抓住}}{{He quickly grasped the main idea of the lesson.}}
{{grave}}{{/ɡreɪv}}{{adj./n. 严重的； grave；坟墓}}{{The patient is in a grave condition.}}
{{grieve}}{{/ɡriːv}}{{v. 悲伤； grieve；哀悼}}{{She grieved the loss of her father.}}
{{gross}}{{/ɡrəʊs}}{{adj. 总的； gross； gross；粗鲁的}}{{The gross profit was $5 million.}}
{{guarantee}}{{/ˌɡærənˈtiː}}{{v./n. 保证； guarantee；保修}}{{The product comes with a two-year guarantee.}}
{{guard}}{{/ɡɑːd}}{{n./v. 守卫； guard；保护}}{{The guard stood at the entrance of the building.}}
{{guide}}{{/ɡaɪd}}{{v./n. 指导； guide；指南}}{{The teacher guided the students through the experiment.}}
{{guilty}}{{/ˈɡɪlti}}{{adj. 有罪的； guilty；内疚的}}{{The jury found him guilty of fraud.}}
{{halt}}{{/hɔːlt}}{{v./n. 停止； halt；暂停}}{{The train came to a halt.}}
{{handle}}{{/ˈhændl}}{{v./n. 处理； handle；手柄}}{{She handled the situation with great skill.}}
{{harbor}}{{/ˈhɑːbər}}{{n./v. 港口； harbor；怀有}}{{The ship arrived at the harbor.}}
{{harmony}}{{/ˈhɑːməni}}{{n. 和谐； harmony；融洽}}{{The community lives in harmony.}}
{{harsh}}{{/hɑːʃ}}{{adj. 严厉的； harsh；恶劣的}}{{The harsh winter made travel difficult.}}
{{harvest}}{{/ˈhɑːvɪst}}{{n./v. 收获； harvest；收割}}{{The farmers celebrated a good harvest.}}
{{hazard}}{{/ˈhæzəd}}{{n./v. 危险； hazard；冒…的风险}}{{Smoking is a health hazard.}}
{{heal}}{{/hiːl}}{{v. 治愈； heal；痊愈}}{{The wound took a long time to heal.}}
{{hesitate}}{{/ˈhezɪteɪt}}{{v. 犹豫； hesitate}}{{Don't hesitate to ask for help.}}
{{highlight}}{{/ˈhaɪlaɪt}}{{v./n. 强调； highlight；亮点}}{{The report highlights the need for reform.}}
{{hint}}{{/hɪnt}}{{n./v. 暗示； hint；提示}}{{She gave a hint about her plans.}}
{{horizon}}{{/həˈraɪzn}}{{n. 地平线； horizon；视野}}{{The sun disappeared below the horizon.}}
{{hostile}}{{/ˈhɒstaɪl}}{{adj. 敌意的； hostile；不利的}}{{The audience was hostile to the speaker.}}
{{household}}{{/ˈhaʊshəʊld}}{{n./adj. 家庭； household；家喻户晓的}}{{The product is a household name.}}
{{humble}}{{/ˈhʌmbl}}{{adj. 谦虚的； humble；卑微的}}{{Despite his success, he remains humble.}}
{{identical}}{{/aɪˈdentɪkl}}{{adj. 相同的； identical；一模一样的}}{{The two paintings are almost identical.}}
